# =============================================================================
# INERT. Docker never reads this file. Nothing you add here excludes anything.
# =============================================================================
# Docker resolves .dockerignore from the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, and every build of
# this image uses the repo root as context — it has to, because the Dockerfile
# does `COPY shared /app/shared`. So the file that actually governs what reaches
# the daemon is the repo-root ../../.dockerignore. Add exclusions THERE.
#
# Code review 2026-08-07 (CICD-6) proposed renaming this to
# `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, which BuildKit does honour. That was rejected after
# reading the patterns below, and the reason is worth keeping:
#
#   A `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` REPLACES the context-root file for that build
#   rather than adding to it. Every pattern here is written relative to THIS
#   directory — `tests/`, `.env`, `.venv/` — so against a repo-root context
#   `tests/` would match only ./tests/ and `.env` only ./.env. Activating this
#   file would therefore switch OFF the root file's `**/.env`, `**/*.env` and
#   `services/*/.venv/` rules, and start shipping real credential files into the
#   image. That is a worse outcome than the file doing nothing, and it is not
#   obvious from reading either file alone.
#
#   Making the rename safe means rewriting all four of these as context-root
#   patterns, at which point they are four copies of ../../.dockerignore, which
#   is the drift the root file exists to prevent.
#
# Kept, not deleted, because the header is the finding: someone WILL open this
# file expecting it to work, and this is where they need to be told it does not.
# ops/ci/check_env_parity.py guards the sibling class of silent config.
#
# Historical contents follow, unchanged, so `git log` still explains them.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Virtualenvs and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dev artefacts
tests/
*.log
*.err

# Git
.git/
.gitignore

# Docs
README.md
*.md

# Node (shouldn't be here but just in case)
node_modules/
